+### Opt-in AIOps host bridge
+
+`initialize` can negotiate the private `aiops-dsh-bridge.v1` extension and receive an exact host-supplied `aiopsTools` surface. The server registers only proxy tools for those schemas and restricts each bridged Agent to that same name set. A proxy call is a server-to-client JSON-RPC request (`aiops.tool.dispatch`); the host must send the result only after its own dispatcher, policy, approval, and cancellation path settles. The extension does not grant the model or DSH process authority to execute a host tool.
+
+The extension adds `turnId` to `session/prompt` and committed `session.event` notifications, plus `session/cancel` for the exact active Go turn, `session/replay` after a durable event cursor, transient `assistant.stream` frames, and `aiops.tool.cancel` for an aborted proxy request. A prompt receipt and `session.status: idle` remain non-terminal signals. Replay contains durable Session events only; stream frames are not durable. The host must persist event sequence and attribution atomically, deduplicate by session and sequence, and recover a tail before deciding the DSH turn settled. After a process restart, a configured session-persistence backend lets the server resume the stored Session; an interrupted Agent turn is repaired by the Agent runtime, and the host must never infer that a mutation should be retried from replay.
+
