-- **No protocol-version negotiation** — the handshake carries only `serverInfo.version` (`0.0.1`, unvalidated by clients); pre-release stance, no compatibility promise.
-- **No cancel or session-close methods** — a client abandons a turn by closing the runtime process; see the [JSON-RPC serving plugin](../server/README.md).
-- **Server→client requests are a dead capability** — the transport supports them, but the server never sends one; the Python SDK's responder surface exists for future approval flows.
+- **The stock SDK protocol has no general protocol-version negotiation or cancel method** — the AIOps extension is separately opted into by exact version and does not add a general session-close operation.
+- **The opt-in host bridge is not part of the stock TypeScript or Python SDK surface** — a host must implement its tool dispatcher and persist event cursors; an unrecognized or missing extension capability must fail initialization.
+- **The extension does not provide business-level exactly-once execution** — Go must keep its idempotency ledger and treat ambiguous mutation outcomes as pending verification; replay never authorizes automatic execution.
